        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Timur</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1320 CE – 1405 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">in the 1320s, near Kesh (now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrisabz">Shahrisabz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a>; son of Taraghai, a noble of the Turkicised Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barlas">Barlas</a> tribe; later Timurid histories give 8 April 1336</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">17 or 18 February 1405, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otrar">Farab</a> beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syr-darya">Syr Darya</a>, of illness during a winter campaign against Ming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>; buried in the Gur-e-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">Amir</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barlas">Barlas</a> from about 1360; sovereign at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkh">Balkh</a> from about 1370, ruling as amir and güregen (royal son-in-law) in the name of puppet Chagatayid khans; styled Sahib Qiran, 'Lord of the Conjunction'</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>; wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-delhi-1398">sack of Delhi</a> (1398); the sacks of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>; the defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a> (1402); patronage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a> and of scholars; the Timurid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a></span></div>
